WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.292
Squid Game is
the South Korean thriller

00:00:02.375 --> 00:00:03.833
taking the world by storm

00:00:03.917 --> 00:00:05.708
and,
if you're anything like us,

00:00:05.792 --> 00:00:08.333
you've consumed the
whole series as hungrily as

00:00:08.417 --> 00:00:10.833
the contestants licking
that tasty honeycomb candy.

00:00:11.458 --> 00:00:13.333
Now that you've survived
all six games,

00:00:13.417 --> 00:00:15.458
you're probably left
with many questions.

00:00:15.542 --> 00:00:16.958
Thankfully,
you don't have to risk

00:00:17.042 --> 00:00:19.458
sneaking into a top secret
island to get answers,

00:00:19.542 --> 00:00:21.042
as we've got you covered.

00:00:21.125 --> 00:00:22.583
Beware of spoilers

00:00:22.667 --> 00:00:24.625
and let the games begin.

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:29.792
Is Squid Game based on
a book?

00:00:30.292 --> 00:00:32.708
With its shocking twists
and iconic uniforms,

00:00:32.792 --> 00:00:35.083
you might think the story
was pulled from a book

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:36.625
or manga, but it's not.

00:00:36.708 --> 00:00:38.458
It's the
entirely fictional creation

00:00:38.542 --> 00:00:40.875
of writer-director
Hwang Dong-hyuk,

00:00:40.958 --> 00:00:44.000
who actually wrote the story
way back in 2008.

00:00:44.083 --> 00:00:46.583
He told Variety
that he did take inspiration

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:48.958
from Japanese comics
and animation,

00:00:49.042 --> 00:00:51.167
saying that he spent
a long time reading manga

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.125
like Battle Royale
and Liar Game

00:00:53.208 --> 00:00:54.875
and wondering
what it would be like

00:00:54.958 --> 00:00:57.458
to take part in those
deadly challenges himself.

00:00:57.542 --> 00:01:00.625
However, where those stories
had complex rules,

00:01:00.708 --> 00:01:03.792
he wanted to base Squid Game
on childhood games instead

00:01:03.875 --> 00:01:05.042
and, because of that,

00:01:05.125 --> 00:01:08.125
well, we'll never look at
marbles the same way again.

00:01:08.208 --> 00:01:09.958
Who stars in Squid Game?

00:01:10.542 --> 00:01:12.167
While the cast
of the show are

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:13.333
well-known in South Korea,

00:01:13.417 --> 00:01:15.167
many international viewers
are asking:

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:16.833
who stars in Squid Game?

00:01:16.917 --> 00:01:19.292
Our down on his luck hero,
Seong Gi-hun,

00:01:19.375 --> 00:01:22.750
is played by TV and
film veteran Lee Jung-jae,

00:01:22.833 --> 00:01:25.208
who is best known here
for his roles in New World

00:01:25.292 --> 00:01:26.417
and Il Mare,

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:28.542
which was remade
as the Sandra Bullock

00:01:28.625 --> 00:01:31.625
and Keanu Reeves time travel
romance The Lake House.

00:01:31.708 --> 00:01:32.917
Park Hae-soo plays

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.958
the duplicitous
financial investor

00:01:35.042 --> 00:01:36.333
Cho Sang-woo

00:01:36.417 --> 00:01:38.625
insert your own boos
and hisses here.

00:01:38.708 --> 00:01:40.667
You can see Park
in Prison Playbook

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:41.917
and he's due to appear in

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.542
the Korean remake
of Money Heist,

00:01:43.625 --> 00:01:45.167
where he'll play Berlin.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:47.958
He must be drawn to projects
with red jumpsuits.

00:01:48.042 --> 00:01:49.500
Amazingly, Hoyeon Jung,

00:01:49.583 --> 00:01:52.500
who plays North Korean
defector Kang Sae-byeok

00:01:52.583 --> 00:01:54.833
makes her acting debut
in Squid Game.

00:01:54.917 --> 00:01:57.292
The former model is really
jumping into the deep end

00:01:57.375 --> 00:01:59.125
with
these intense death games.

00:01:59.208 --> 00:02:01.333
And ageing contestant
Oh Il-nam

00:02:01.417 --> 00:02:03.625
is played by Oh Yeong-su,

00:02:03.708 --> 00:02:04.917
best known for his role
as a monk

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.042
in Spring, Summer, Fall,
Winter… and Spring.

00:02:08.125 --> 00:02:12.375
We made a pinkie promise
to be each other's gganbu.

00:02:12.458 --> 00:02:15.000
Is Squid Game a real game
in Korea?

00:02:15.083 --> 00:02:17.708
And, by this,
we mean the playground game,

00:02:17.792 --> 00:02:20.083
not the whole locking
456 people

00:02:20.167 --> 00:02:21.625
in a battle to the death.

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:24.042
Happily,
this bit isn't real,

00:02:24.125 --> 00:02:25.500
but the childhood pastime

00:02:25.583 --> 00:02:27.458
that is played in
the show's opening moments

00:02:27.542 --> 00:02:30.042
and in the final episode
definitely is.

00:02:30.542 --> 00:02:32.750
Squid Game involves a team
of defenders trying to stop

00:02:32.833 --> 00:02:34.125
a team of attackers from

00:02:34.208 --> 00:02:36.333
reaching a square
in the outline of a squid

00:02:36.417 --> 00:02:37.583
drawn on the floor,

00:02:37.667 --> 00:02:39.458
with the attackers
stuck on one leg

00:02:39.542 --> 00:02:41.708
until they cross
the middle of the squid.

00:02:41.792 --> 00:02:44.250
The game was popular
in the 1970s and 80s

00:02:44.333 --> 00:02:45.208
and is one of director

00:02:45.292 --> 00:02:46.625
Hwang Dong-hyuk's favourites

00:02:46.708 --> 00:02:48.458
from his playground days.

00:02:48.542 --> 00:02:50.042
He told the Korea Herald

00:02:50.125 --> 00:02:51.625
that it is:
"a perfect metaphor

00:02:51.708 --> 00:02:53.708
of our
highly competitive society".

00:02:53.792 --> 00:02:55.000
In the real life version,

00:02:55.083 --> 00:02:56.917
people aren't allowed to
use knives,

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.208
but then real life
tug of war isn't played

00:02:59.292 --> 00:03:01.333
above a giant pit, either.

00:03:01.417 --> 00:03:03.208
As with
so many childhood games,

00:03:03.292 --> 00:03:04.958
rules vary from kid to kid

00:03:05.042 --> 00:03:07.042
and different groups have
different names

00:03:07.125 --> 00:03:08.333
for different rituals.

00:03:08.417 --> 00:03:09.500
The secret inspector.

00:03:10.333 --> 00:03:11.958
For whatever reason,

00:03:12.042 --> 00:03:14.833
we called that
the secret inspector.

00:03:14.917 --> 00:03:16.625
But, with the success
of the show,

00:03:16.708 --> 00:03:17.958
expect squid game
to be flooding

00:03:18.042 --> 00:03:20.208
international playgrounds
soon.

00:03:20.292 --> 00:03:22.667
Is the honeycomb game real?

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:25.625
Easily the most delicious
challenge in Squid Game,

00:03:25.708 --> 00:03:27.625
it's not like
the cafeteria food is

00:03:27.708 --> 00:03:28.708
much to write home about.

00:03:28.792 --> 00:03:30.500
The honeycomb game is,
indeed,

00:03:30.583 --> 00:03:32.458
based on
another Korean pastime.

00:03:32.542 --> 00:03:34.375
Known as dalgona candy,

00:03:34.458 --> 00:03:35.750
the snack is
traditionally made

00:03:35.833 --> 00:03:37.250
from sugar and baking soda

00:03:37.333 --> 00:03:39.208
and has an image
pressed into it

00:03:39.292 --> 00:03:40.542
with a biscuit cutter.

00:03:40.625 --> 00:03:41.958
Children then
attempt to nibble

00:03:42.042 --> 00:03:43.292
around the edges
of the picture

00:03:43.375 --> 00:03:45.208
to cut it
without breaking it.

00:03:45.292 --> 00:03:48.500
Again, Squid Game adds
a sinister punishment

00:03:48.583 --> 00:03:49.542
for snapping the image,

00:03:49.625 --> 00:03:51.208
but the basics
of the challenge

00:03:51.292 --> 00:03:52.667
are true to real life.

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:53.667
So, top tip:

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:56.375
if you ever find yourself in
a South Korean playground,

00:03:56.458 --> 00:03:58.792
pick the simplest image
possible.

00:03:58.875 --> 00:04:02.333
How much is
46.5 billion won?

00:04:02.417 --> 00:04:03.750
Now for the
million dollar question

00:04:03.833 --> 00:04:07.042
or, rather, the
45.6 billion won question:

00:04:07.125 --> 00:04:10.333
how much is
45.6 billion won worth?

00:04:10.417 --> 00:04:11.958
That's the prize
up for grabs

00:04:12.042 --> 00:04:14.375
if you manage to survive
all six of the death games

00:04:14.458 --> 00:04:15.958
and walk away the victor.

00:04:16.042 --> 00:04:18.292
It sounds like
a life-changing amount

00:04:18.375 --> 00:04:19.708
and it certainly is.

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:23.625
At today's rates,
it equals $38.6 million

00:04:23.708 --> 00:04:26.333
or £28.2 million.

00:04:26.417 --> 00:04:29.083
There are 456 players
in the survival game

00:04:29.167 --> 00:04:31.375
and each death adds
100 million won

00:04:31.458 --> 00:04:32.583
to the piggybank.

00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:34.833
That makes the price
of a human life

00:04:34.917 --> 00:04:38.625
$84,000 or £62,000.

00:04:39.125 --> 00:04:40.792
Just after one game
of red light, green light,

00:04:40.875 --> 00:04:44.375
the prize money sits
at 25.5 billion won,

00:04:44.458 --> 00:04:48.583
$21.5 million
or £15.9 million.

00:04:48.667 --> 00:04:51.208
Suddenly, you understand
why so many people voted to

00:04:51.292 --> 00:04:53.875
stay in the game after
that harrowing first round.

00:04:53.958 --> 00:04:55.250
The most important thing is

00:04:55.833 --> 00:04:57.542
you get the prize money
on a credit card

00:04:57.625 --> 00:04:59.167
rather than
heaving the pig home.

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:01.375
What do the business card
symbols mean?

00:05:01.875 --> 00:05:03.875
Circles, triangles
and squares

00:05:03.958 --> 00:05:05.750
appear everywhere
in Squid Game.

00:05:05.833 --> 00:05:06.708
And, no,

00:05:06.792 --> 00:05:08.500
they aren't a sneaky advert
for PlayStation.

00:05:08.583 --> 00:05:10.708
Found on the business cards
used to lure players

00:05:10.792 --> 00:05:11.667
into the game,

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:13.542
the circle, triangle
and square

00:05:13.625 --> 00:05:16.042
are letters of Hangul,
the Korean alphabet.

00:05:16.125 --> 00:05:17.958
The circle represents "O",

00:05:18.042 --> 00:05:20.500
the triangle forms
part of the letter "J"

00:05:20.583 --> 00:05:22.333
an the square stands for
an "M".

00:05:22.417 --> 00:05:24.583
Taken together,
they read "OJM",

00:05:24.667 --> 00:05:27.083
which form part of the
Korean name for Squid Game,

00:05:27.167 --> 00:05:28.333
Ojingeo Geim.

00:05:28.417 --> 00:05:29.792
They also double up
as shapes

00:05:29.875 --> 00:05:31.292
taken from the floor pattern

00:05:31.375 --> 00:05:33.250
used to play squid game
itself.

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:35.875
What is the red light,
green light doll based on?

00:05:35.958 --> 00:05:38.542
In a series full of
instantly iconic characters

00:05:38.625 --> 00:05:39.500
and settings,

00:05:39.583 --> 00:05:41.333
none made
the same impact on us

00:05:41.417 --> 00:05:43.500
as the creepy robotic doll.

00:05:43.583 --> 00:05:45.542
-Hey.
-What?

00:05:45.625 --> 00:05:47.542
-Look over there.
-What is that?

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:49.458
It looks really freaky.

00:05:49.542 --> 00:05:51.583
Damn, that thing has
a freaking huge head.

00:05:51.667 --> 00:05:52.583
In the show,

00:05:52.667 --> 00:05:54.417
the doll controls red light,
green light,

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:57.375
spotting any contestants
who move after the song

00:05:57.458 --> 00:05:59.750
and dooming them
to a terrible fate.

00:05:59.833 --> 00:06:02.125
But, incredibly,
this terrifying statue

00:06:02.208 --> 00:06:03.542
wasn't built for Squid Game.

00:06:03.625 --> 00:06:05.542
It exists in real life.

00:06:05.625 --> 00:06:08.000
The doll belongs to
a horse carriage museum

00:06:08.083 --> 00:06:09.167
called Macha Land

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:10.583
found in
the South Korean village

00:06:10.667 --> 00:06:12.083
in Jincheon county.

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:17.750
At the museum,

00:06:17.833 --> 00:06:20.417
she serves
the slightly less scary role

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:22.125
of welcoming visitors
to the museum,

00:06:22.208 --> 00:06:24.208
so feel free
to move all you like.

00:06:24.292 --> 00:06:26.667
Is Squid Game dubbed?

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:28.458
Made in South Korea,

00:06:28.542 --> 00:06:30.958
you can enjoy Squid Game
in the original Korean

00:06:31.042 --> 00:06:33.625
with subtitles or with
an English language dub.

00:06:33.708 --> 00:06:34.750
But, I'm afraid that

00:06:34.833 --> 00:06:36.500
whichever version
you listen to,

00:06:36.583 --> 00:06:38.917
the show is
no less heart-breaking.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:40.042
Thank you.

00:06:42.708 --> 00:06:44.083
You made all this

00:06:46.167 --> 00:06:47.792
a good experience.

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:51.042
Will there be a second
season of Squid Game?

00:06:51.125 --> 00:06:52.500
Well,
we don't know that yet,

00:06:52.583 --> 00:06:55.167
but there's certainly room
for more stories to be told.

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:56.583
Until we find out more,

00:06:56.667 --> 00:06:59.292
we'll just keep re-watching
episode six

00:06:59.375 --> 00:07:00.750
and crying ourselves
to sleep.

00:07:01.333 --> 00:07:02.667
Did you enjoy Squid Game?

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:04.500
And, if you were running
the contest,

00:07:04.583 --> 00:07:07.083
which playground games would
you turn into challenges

00:07:07.167 --> 00:07:08.083
for the contestants?

00:07:08.167 --> 00:07:10.750
Share your most devious
thoughts in the comments

00:07:10.833 --> 00:07:13.667
and remember to subscribe to
Still Watching Netflix

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:15.167
right now for more videos

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:17.250
about your favourite shows
and movies.

